fix: history is never loaded for an already-read buffer

`restoreScrollPosition` returns as soon as the buffer has no rendered child, which is
exactly the case where history has to be requested: `onScrollTop` is never reached and
the buffer stays empty until you switch away and back.

diff --git a/components/scroll-manager.js b/components/scroll-manager.js
index 13ee0e8..35ebd84 100644
--- a/components/scroll-manager.js
+++ b/components/scroll-manager.js
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ export default class ScrollManager extends Component {
 	restoreScrollPosition() {
 		let target = this.props.target.current;
 		if (!target.firstChild) {
+			// Nothing rendered yet: that is precisely when history is needed.
+			this.props.onScrollTop();
 			return;
 		}
 
